# seatd -- libseat, the seat management library weston's DRM backend links.
#
# SEATD IS REQUIRED BY WESTON, NOT SELECTED, and the distinction is the whole
# justification for this package -- so it is taken from the code that imposes it
# rather than from a claim about defaults. weston 14.0.2, libweston/meson.build:
#
#     if get_option('backend-drm')
#         dep_libseat = dependency('libseat', version: '>= 0.4')
#
# Unconditional whenever the DRM backend is on, with no option guarding it.
# There is no -Dlauncher-libseat in weston 14 despite it being an easy thing to
# assume exists. 0.9.1 clears the >= 0.4 floor comfortably.
#
# Corroborated by LINKAGE rather than by a distro's BuildRequires: Alpine's
# weston-backend-drm links exactly libdisplay-info.so.3, libseat.so.1,
# libdrm.so.2, libgbm.so.1, libinput.so.10, libpixman-1.so.0, libudev.so.1 and
# libwayland-*. Of those, only libseat and libdisplay-info were missing here.
#
# WHY THIS FITS DUCT WITHOUT A WORKAROUND, worth recording because the reflex on
# reading "seat management" is to reach for systemd. libseat has three backends.
# The LOGIND backend speaks the interface elogind already implements. The
# BUILTIN backend is root-only and is what the live ISO uses, since the session
# there is root. The seatd DAEMON is the third, for a multi-user installed
# system without elogind. That is the second time elogind has quietly done what
# systemd would have been assumed necessary for; the first was pam_elogind
# creating /run/user/<uid>.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://git.sr.ht/~kennylevinsen/seatd/archive/0.9.1.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=819979c922a0be258aed133d93920bce6a3d3565a60588d6d372ce9db2712cd3
SRC_DIR=seatd-0.9.1

# Every option below was read from meson_options.txt and meson.build IN THIS
# TARBALL, with its upstream default recorded beside it. An option left unnamed
# is indistinguishable from an option nobody considered.
#
# TWO OF THESE ARE LOAD-BEARING AND THEY FAIL IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS. One
# default is dangerous by being permissive, the other by being restrictive, and
# NEITHER PRODUCES AN ERROR. That is why both are named, and why deleting either
# as redundant would break a different configuration:
#
# -Dlibseat-logind=elogind. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS 'auto'. Under auto, meson.build
# takes
#     logind = dependency(['libelogind', 'libsystemd'], required: false)
# -- required:FALSE. If neither is found the logind backend is simply omitted:
# libseat still compiles, still installs, and still works perfectly ON THE LIVE
# ISO, because the session there is root and falls through to the builtin
# backend. It then fails for a normal user on an installed system. Naming
# elogind takes the other branch,
#     logind = dependency('lib@0@'.format(get_option('libseat-logind')))
# which is required by default, so a missing libelogind becomes a hard configure
# error instead of a silent absence discovered by the first non-root user.
# The explicit value IS the assertion; that is why this recipe needs no
# install-time check for it.
#
# -Dlibseat-builtin=enabled. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS 'disabled', so this one is
# load-bearing in the opposite direction. The builtin backend is THE ONE THE
# LIVE ISO ACTUALLY USES. Trusting the default would ship libseat with the
# logind and seatd backends only -- weston would start correctly on an installed
# system with elogind, and fail on the live medium, which is the configuration
# tested first.
#
# -Dlibseat-seatd=enabled and -Dserver=enabled are both already the defaults.
# Named anyway so the three-backend decision is legible in one place rather than
# being half default and half explicit.
#
# -Dexamples=disabled is already the default. Named for the same reason.
#
# -Dman-pages=disabled. The spelling is 'man-pages', hyphenated, and the TYPE IS
# 'feature' rather than boolean -- so 'disabled' is correct and -Dman-pages=false
# would be rejected outright. scdoc is not packaged and is not worth packaging
# for a handful of man pages; meson.build takes it as
# dependency('scdoc', required: get_option('man-pages'), ...).
#
# NOT SET: -Ddefaultpath, a string defaulting to '' which selects seatd's own
# default socket location. Nothing here needs it moved.
MESON_ARGS="-Dlibseat-logind=elogind -Dlibseat-seatd=enabled -Dlibseat-builtin=enabled \
-Dserver=enabled -Dexamples=disabled -Dman-pages=disabled"
